+# Version Numbering Scheme
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Semantic Versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH) for release version numbers: MAJOR is incremented for breaking changes, MINOR for backward-compatible features, and PATCH for bug fixes. The rationale on record is that this gives users clear compatibility signals, so they can tell whether an update is safe to adopt (patch/minor) or requires changes on their side (major), and plan upgrades accordingly.
